{
  "title": "Keep old shopping-list submissions from dismissing a reopened sheet",
  "description": "AddToShoppingListModal.tsx schedules props.onClose with an untracked 1500ms setTimeout after a successful submission. \
Closing with Escape/backdrop and reopening before that timer fires lets the previous submission close the new presentation. \
A response arriving after dismissal can also schedule this stale close. \
AddToShoppingListSheet.swift similarly uses DispatchQueue.main.asyncAfter to set the shared isPresented binding to false without tying the delayed close to that presentation. \
Scope completion state and delayed dismissal to the originating presentation, cancel or invalidate pending timers on close/unmount, and test close/reopen during both pending submission and success on web and iOS. \
AddToMealPlanModal.tsx already tracks its close timer and provides a useful comparison.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
